---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const talkSrc = "/media/durable-podcast-render-talk.mp4";
const talkPoster = "/media/durable-podcast-render-talk-poster.jpg";
const demoSrc = "/media/durable-podcast-render-demo.mp4";
const demoPoster = "/media/durable-podcast-render-demo-poster.jpg";
const deckUrl = "/durable-podcast-render/deck.html";
---

<PageLayout
  title="A podcast render that survives its worker"
  kicker="Durable execution"
  description="A durable-execution walkthrough: moving podcast-render progress from the request to the chunk with Temporal."
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class="dpr stack stack-l">
    <div class="dpr__premise stack measure">
      <p>
        The system is a podcast renderer: it takes digest text, sends it to a
        text-to-speech provider in chunks, and stitches the pieces into one
        audio file.
      </p>
      <p>
        In the old shape, one HTTP request owns the whole job. It keeps the
        finished chunks in memory and records nothing about partial progress.
        When the process dies at chunk six of eight, those six paid-for chunks
        vanish. Recovery restarts at chunk one and pays the provider again for
        work already done.
      </p>
      <p>
        Temporal moves the unit of durable progress from the request to the
        chunk. Each finished chunk is recorded in workflow history, so you can
        kill the process, kill the worker, and a replacement still replays what
        completed and continues from chunk seven. A retryable provider error
        retries only the chunk that failed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="dpr__media">
      <video
        class="dpr__video"
        controls
        preload="metadata"
        poster={talkPoster}
      >
        <source src={talkSrc} type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
      <figcaption class="dpr__caption muted">The full talk, ~20 min</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure class="dpr__media">
      <video
        class="dpr__video"
        controls
        preload="metadata"
        poster={demoPoster}
      >
        <source src={demoSrc} type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
      <figcaption class="dpr__caption muted">
        The demo, ~8 min: two process kills, one injected failure, eight chunks,
        one file
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p class="cluster" style="--cluster-gap: var(--space-m)">
      <a class="dpr__cta" href={deckUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Open the slides ↗
      </a>
    </p>

    <p class="secondary measure">
      Reproduction: the live sequence runs against a local Temporal server,
      PostgreSQL, and object storage with a deterministic TTS adapter, so it
      makes no provider calls and its retry counts are assertable.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .dpr__media {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
  }
  .dpr__video {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    max-height: 70vh;
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    display: block;
  }
  .dpr__caption {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
  .dpr__cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    padding: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-m);
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    color: var(--color-text);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
  }
  .dpr__cta:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
</style>
